ing the temperature on each side of the bed in real time. Why? So you and your partner can consistently hit your ideal deep restorative sleep range and wake up feeling truly refreshed. Refreshed and recovered. Use my code ROGAN at 8sleep.com/rogan for up to $350 off the Pod 5 Ultra. The best part is that you get 30 days to try it at home and return it if you don't like it. But I got a feeling your body will love your investment in better sleep. That's code ROGAN at 8sleep.com/rogan."], [0, "Well, yeah, I mean, I was Oh, I was, I was like always the junior of the group a lot of times because like I said, I've, you know, I've been on my own since I was 14. I haven't grown an inch since I was 13, 14. I was, I looked like a grown-ass man, right? I was fighting in tournaments at 15 against, you know, uh, uh, grown men, like, you know, fighting heavyweight at that time. But I was always hanging with older people. Kind of, you know, kind of like I got away with kind of living as an adult early on. Because like, you know\u2014 Did you work? Yeah, well, I was teaching a karate class. What was happening, see, I used to hang out at this community center in the hood. At this time, I moved from Brooklyn to Bridgeport, Connecticut, right?"], [1, "Bridgeport's a tough neighborhood."], [0, "Yeah, yeah, it was a lot of people don't know. Yeah, we had the top murder rate per capita, man."], [1, "Like, Bridgeport's rough."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["street violence", "personal safety", "self reliance", "childhood adversity", "tough neighborhoods", "urban life", "crime", "murder rates", "community centers", "martial arts", "karate", "fighting tournaments", "early adulthood", "work experience", "sleep technology"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778200609.1435437, "duration_sec": 2.716156005859375, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[3, "They really\u2014 they really only come when they have to."], [1, "Yeah."], [3, "The reason they don't like it is because of the immigration, the way they treat them when they're crossing. They always get harassed. Yeah. When they're going back to America, they get harassed. So they get tired of that."], [1, "Los Algodones has long been set up for the benefit of Americans, and the journey Americans take to cross into Molar City has always been a simple one. But of course, the journey in the opposite direction is much more complicated. Can I ask you a question that might sound\u2014 I don't know, I don't know how you'll take it, but I'll ask it anyway. You can tell me how you react to it. I've heard from Americans and Canadians, like people describing what it's like to go down to Los Algodones, and people describe just walking freely through the border, like just 5 minutes, no need to even show a passport. And I, I'm just curious what that's like for you on your end, knowing that you were kicked out, and yet part of your job is to interact daily with I don't know, hundreds of people who just walk so freely across this border, you know?"], [3, "The way I see it is like this. Since I am from the border and we lived in America, we went to school in America, what happens is that when I see people coming from America and I see myself that I can't go back, which is like literally Right there, I can see my mom's house from right here."], [1, "Oh, wow."], [3, "That's the hardest thing to see. I see my house. I got the Colorado River, and I can literally see the water tank at the reservation, and then I can see all the way to the Yuma hospital on 24th Street, and then I kind of know more or less where my mom's house is over here. If I had a drone, I could fly it over there and and look at and go, \"Ouch.\"."], [1, "Yeah."], [3, "That's how close I am. That's not easy. It's very hard for me."], [1, "It's 5:00 AM in Algodones. The sky is still dark, not quite sunrise, and Alberto is shuffling around the house, getting ready for for work. The streets are mostly quiet at this hour, just the sound of other promoters and vendors setting up, setting the stage for Molar City. By 6:00 AM, he's at his post. The border opens and the Americans descend. They walk in the shadow of the 30-foot wall that divides them. Crossing the very threshold Alberto cannot."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Society & Culture"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["immigration", "border crossing", "deportation", "discrimination", "harassment", "identity", "family separation", "united states mexico border", "travel", "american tourists", "indigenous communities", "work", "inequality", "border wall"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778200663.7277906, "duration_sec": 1.1837825775146484, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Las \u00faltimas noticias del mundo las encuentras en el podcast de Noticias Univisi\u00f3n 24-7. Esc\u00fachanos en el podcast Noticias Univisi\u00f3n 24-7 en Euphoria App, Apple Podcast, Spotify y el canal de YouTube de Euphoria Podcast o donde sea que escuchan sus podcasts. Bienvenidos al podcast del noticiero Univisi\u00f3n Edici\u00f3n Nocturna. Aqu\u00ed escuchar\u00e1s todas las noticias que necesitas saber para estar informado de los hechos m\u00e1s importantes d\u00eda con d\u00eda."], [0, "Estas son las noticias que necesitas saber antes de que termine tu d\u00eda. Caos en los aeropuertos de costa a costa. Millones de pasajeros sufren largas filas por la falta de personal al tiempo que ya comienzan a llegar los agentes de ICE a las terminales. Al menos dos muertos y m\u00e1s de 40 heridos es el saldo de un choque entre un avi\u00f3n de Air Canada y un cami\u00f3n de bomberos en el aeropuerto La Guardia de Nueva York."], [0, "\u00bfSe imagina estar en su casa y que caiga un meteorito a 35 mil millas por hora? Una residente de Texas fue testigo de este fen\u00f3meno de la naturaleza y tenemos sus reacciones. Se acerca la fecha l\u00edmite para declarar sus impuestos y les explicamos cu\u00e1les son las causas por las cuales el IRS podr\u00eda auditar su declaraci\u00f3n. Este es un noticiero N m\u00e1s Univisi\u00f3n Edici\u00f3n Nocturna con Paulina Zodi."], [0, "Hola, \u00bfqu\u00e9 tal? Muy buenas noches. Les saluda Elian Zidane hoy por Paulina Zodi. El inicio del Spring Break ha sido marcado por el caos en distintos aeropuertos del pa\u00eds. Entre los m\u00e1s afectados est\u00e1n los aeropuertos de Houston, Nueva York La Guardia, Chicago y Atlanta."], [0, "filas que salen hasta la calle y tiempos de espera cada vez mayores. Se han registrado tambi\u00e9n debido a la ola de ausencias y renuncias de agentes de la Agencia de Seguridad en el Transporte, la TSA por su acr\u00f3nimo en ingl\u00e9s. Esto se debe tambi\u00e9n al cierre parcial del gobierno y del Departamento de Seguridad Nacional. Tan solo el s\u00e1bado, vea esto, 3.200 agentes de la TSA faltaron a su trabajo y m\u00e1s de 400 han renunciado desde febrero. Romy de Fr\u00edas,"], [0, "Nos ampl\u00eda."], [0, "docenas de aeropuertos en los Estados Unidos han colapsado ante la falta de agentes de seguridad en el transporte. En el aeropuerto de Hartfield-Jackson, en Atlanta, m\u00e1s de un tercio de los empleados de TSA se ausentaron. Es por eso que el presidente Donald Trump ha desplegado agentes de ICE en 13 aeropuertos, incluyendo este. Esta viajera lleva dos d\u00edas esperando su vuelo. S\u00ed funciona, pero causa miedo. Muchas personas ayer que superaron buscaron c\u00f3mo irse por tierra."], [0, "Todo donde est\u00e1 ICE causa miedo. La presencia de los agentes migratorios en el aeropuerto de Atlanta ha causado miedo y descontento, tal como lo expresa este grupo de manifestantes. En el aeropuerto de La Guardia, en Nueva York, la fila de pasajeros llegaba hasta el estacionamiento. Hoy uniformados con chalecos de ICE circulan por los pasillos."], [0, "El alcalde de Chicago dijo que se esperan hasta 75 agentes de inmigraci\u00f3n en el aeropuerto O'Hare. Las funciones de los agentes de ICE podr\u00edan variar de acuerdo al aeropuerto, pero se concentrar\u00edan b\u00e1sicamente en la seguridad. Si yo s\u00e9 que el ICE va a venir, yo voy a prevenir venir ac\u00e1."], [0, "Definitivamente. Lorena Granada no est\u00e1 de acuerdo con que agentes de inmigraci\u00f3n est\u00e9n en los aeropuertos, p